# Android (TWA) build artifacts
android/android.keystore
android/keystore-password.txt
# The signing password, written by whoever builds the APK and read by
# `npm run dist:android`. A keystore without its password is a signing identity that
# cannot be used and cannot be replaced: the site's assetlinks.json names its
# fingerprint, so a different keystore means editing and deploying the site as well.
android/keystore.properties
android/app/
android/build/
android/.gradle/
android/gradle.properties
android/settings.gradle
android/build.gradle
android/gradlew
android/gradlew.bat
android/gradle/
android/store_icon.png
android/*.apk
android/*.aab
android/manifest-checksum.txt
android/.idea/

# The installer.
#
# Not in git, and not deployed with the site either: Cloudflare Workers refuses any
# static asset over 25 MiB and the installer is 107 MiB, so putting it here made
# `wrangler deploy` refuse the whole site rather than skip one file. It is served
# from R2 instead, which is what R2 is for — a few megabytes of chat uploads and a
# hundred megabyte installer are the same problem.
#
# Copy it next to the site with:
#   npm run build && copy release\Tody-Game-Hub-1.0.0-setup-x64.exe public\downloads\
# and upload it to the bucket with `npm run dist` followed by the bucket step in the
# deploy notes. Nothing links there at the moment — the menu and the chat's account
# panel hand over the installer from Drive, which is where the build already is — but
# the worker still sets the right headers for it if it is ever served from here.
public/downloads/
